From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: enable BCM-NAT IPv6, expect refresh, and offloadable flag

Add NF_CT_HELPER_F_OFFLOADABLE so BCM-NAT helpers remain compatible
with software flowtable offload while preserving existing helper
rejection for protocol helpers (FTP/SIP/etc.). Generalize BCM fullcone
NAT across both AF_INET and AF_INET6 via bcm_nat_setup_fullcone(),
refresh live expectation timers on reuse and inbound hits, honour
RANDOM/RANDOM_FULLY and RFC 4787 port parity before opposite-parity
fallback, and replace BUG_ON() with WARN_ON_ONCE().

Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff -uNrp a/include/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_helper.h b/include/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_helper.h
--- a/include/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_helper.h	2026-11-23 11:31:56.056887142 +0800
+++ b/include/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_helper.h	2026-11-23 11:31:56.083998665 +0800
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ struct module;
 enum nf_ct_helper_flags {
 	NF_CT_HELPER_F_USERSPACE	= (1 << 0),
 	NF_CT_HELPER_F_CONFIGURED	= (1 << 1),
+	NF_CT_HELPER_F_OFFLOADABLE	= (1 << 2),
 };
 
 #define NF_CT_HELPER_NAME_LEN	16
